{"id": "tea:sivananasiddhiyar:cupakkam.1", "source": "src:sivananasiddhiyar", "location": {"ref": "cupakkam.1"}, "paraphrase": "The Lord performs the five acts — creation, maintenance, destruction, concealment and grace — not for himself but out of compassion, so that souls may exhaust their karma and ripen their mala; even destruction is rest for the souls.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate", "world-fate"], "concepts": ["cpt:five-acts-of-siva"], "terms": ["trm:pancakrtya"], "notes": "Chapter-level reference; exact verse not given.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sivananasiddhiyar:cupakkam.11", "source": "src:sivananasiddhiyar", "location": {"ref": "cupakkam.11"}, "paraphrase": "In liberation the soul does not become Śiva nor perish; it abides inseparable from him, enjoying his bliss, as the malas, which are eternal, lie powerless.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "realized"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:siddhanta-advaita"], "disputes": ["dsp:liberation-identity-or-equality-with-siva", "dsp:mala-substance-or-ignorance"], "notes": "Chapter-level reference.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sivananasiddhiyar:cupakkam.2", "source": "src:sivananasiddhiyar", "location": {"ref": "cupakkam.2"}, "paraphrase": "God's non-duality with souls means not identity but inseparability: he is one with them, different from them and together with them, as the vowel is in the consonants; the Vedic sayings of oneness are to be understood so.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "concepts": ["cpt:siddhanta-advaita"], "disputes": ["dsp:liberation-identity-or-equality-with-siva", "dsp:souls-one-or-distinct"], "notes": "Chapter-level reference.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sivananasiddhiyar:cupakkam.8", "source": "src:sivananasiddhiyar", "location": {"ref": "cupakkam.8"}, "paraphrase": "When the two deeds come into balance and the soul's mala has ripened, Śiva's power descends (catti nipātam) in four grades — very mild, mild, intense and very intense — fitting the soul for caryā, kriyā, yoga or jñāna; Śiva then comes as the guru and initiates.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "teacher-transmission"], "terms": ["trm:iruvinaiyoppu", "trm:malaparipaka", "trm:saktipata"], "concepts": ["cpt:iruvinaiyoppu", "cpt:malaparipaka", "cpt:kinds-of-saktipata"], "paths": ["pth:saiva-siddhanta-four-padas"], "disputes": ["dsp:cause-of-saktipata"], "notes": "Chapter-level reference; the grade-to-path mapping is moderate confidence.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sivananasiddhiyar:cupakkam.8/2", "source": "src:sivananasiddhiyar", "location": {"ref": "cupakkam.8"}, "paraphrase": "The guru initiates in seven ways — by look, touch, word, thought, instruction in the scriptures, yoga, and the fire rite (auttiri) — destroying the accumulated karma; the prārabdha that formed the body is exhausted by experience.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ritual", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual", "knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission", "karma-liberation"], "terms": ["trm:diksa", "trm:prarabdha"], "concepts": ["cpt:kinds-of-diksa"], "practices": ["prc:diksa"], "disputes": ["dsp:does-diksa-liberate"], "notes": "The list of seven kinds is recalled at moderate-low confidence.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sivananasiddhiyar:cupakkam.8/3", "source": "src:sivananasiddhiyar", "location": {"ref": "cupakkam.8"}, "paraphrase": "Caryā, kriyā, yoga and jñāna are four steps; the first three give the lower liberations (sālokya, sāmīpya, sārūpya) and ripen the soul; only jñāna, given by the guru's grace, leads to union (sāyujya). Jñāna itself proceeds by hearing, reflection, clarity and abiding (kēṭṭal, cintittal, teḷital, niṭṭai).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["action", "ritual", "meditation", "knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice", "karma-liberation"], "terms": ["trm:carya", "trm:kriya", "trm:sivayoga", "trm:sivajnana", "trm:salokya", "trm:samipya", "trm:sarupya", "trm:sayujya", "trm:nittai"], "concepts": ["cpt:four-padas", "cpt:four-kinds-of-mukti"], "practices": ["prc:saiva-carya", "prc:saiva-kriya", "prc:saiva-yoga", "prc:saiva-jnana"], "paths": ["pth:saiva-siddhanta-four-padas"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sivananasiddhiyar:parapakkam", "source": "src:sivananasiddhiyar", "location": {"ref": "parapakkam"}, "paraphrase": "The opponents' section sets out in their own terms and then refutes the Lokāyata, the four Buddhist schools, the Jains, the Ājīvikas, the Mīmāṃsakas, the grammarians' word-Brahman, Māyāvāda Vedānta, Bhāskara's view, the Pāñcarātra, the Sāṃkhya and others, as a preparation for the Siddhānta.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["dispute"], "disputes": ["dsp:world-real-or-appearance", "dsp:is-there-a-self"], "concepts": ["cpt:four-circles-of-schools"], "notes": "Fourteen schools are traditionally counted; the list here is partial and moderate confidence.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sivananasiddhiyar:parapakkam.acivaka", "source": "src:sivananasiddhiyar", "location": {"ref": "parapakkam.acivaka"}, "paraphrase": "The Parapakkam includes the Ācīvakam among the schools it refutes.", "tags": {"level": "unmarked", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "unmarked"}, "types": ["dispute"], "concepts": ["cpt:niyativada"], "teachers": ["tch:arunanti"], "reported_by_opponent": true, "notes": "Reported by an opponent: Aruṇanti Civācāriyār (Śaiva Siddhānta). Not checked; from memory.", "coverage": ["B1", "A7"], "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U33-sramana"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U33-sramana"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sivananasiddhiyar:parapakkam.lokayata", "source": "src:sivananasiddhiyar", "location": {"ref": "parapakkam.lokayata"}, "paraphrase": "The Parapakkam opens with the Lōkāyatam: only perception is valid, the four elements alone exist, consciousness arises from their combination, and there is no other world — and refutes it.", "tags": {"level": "unmarked", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "unmarked"}, "types": ["dispute"], "concepts": ["cpt:bhuta-caitanya", "cpt:pratyaksa-only"], "teachers": ["tch:arunanti"], "reported_by_opponent": true, "notes": "Reported by an opponent: Aruṇanti Civācāriyār (Śaiva Siddhānta). Not checked; section order from memory.", "coverage": ["B1", "A7"], "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U33-sramana"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U33-sramana"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
